   199	            // We're doing some trickery here.
   200	            // We reserve 64 extra entries, because we've at most 64 bit to set
   201	            // then we truncate the base to the next base (that we calculated above)
   202	            // We later indiscriminatory write over the len we set but that's OK
   203	            // since we ensure we reserve the needed space
   204	            base.reserve(64);
   205	            let final_len = l + cnt;
